From: clawd20130 <clawd20130@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 18:44:41 +0900
Subject: Screencast: do not exclude the Plasma Mobile shell when it is the recorder

Plasma Mobile records the screen from its own shell process; excluding the recorder's windows
then removed the wallpaper, launcher and panels (a black home screen). Like the portal, the
shell recorder is not excluded; per-window excludeFromCapture still applies. Keyed on the
executable since the round-2 fold (docs/72); it was gated on an environment variable.

Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-09-26
X-Rungic-Status: Pending [generic for Plasma Mobile]
X-Rungic-Tests: L3:recording.quicksetting
X-Rungic-Docs: docs/46
Origin: vendor
---
 src/plugins/screencast/screencastmanager.cpp | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/plugins/screencast/screencastmanager.cpp b/src/plugins/screencast/screencastmanager.cpp
index d30c913..937eef1 100644
--- a/src/plugins/screencast/screencastmanager.cpp
+++ b/src/plugins/screencast/screencastmanager.cpp
@@ -103,7 +103,12 @@ void ScreencastManager::streamWaylandOutput(ScreencastStreamV1Interface *wayland
 
 static std::optional<pid_t> getPid(ScreencastStreamV1Interface *waylandStream)
 {
-    if (waylandStream->connection()->executablePath().contains("xdg-desktop-portal-kde")) {
+    const auto executable = waylandStream->connection()->executablePath();
+    // Plasma Mobile records from its own shell process. Excluding that PID
+    // also removes the wallpaper, launcher and panels, yielding a black home
+    // screen. Keep explicit per-window excludeFromCapture filtering intact.
+    const bool mobileShellRecorder = executable == QStringLiteral("/usr/bin/plasmashell");
+    if (mobileShellRecorder || executable.contains("xdg-desktop-portal-kde")) {
         // HACK to avoid the portal's windows being hidden
         return std::nullopt;
     }
